    "content": "\"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.\nItems, one per line:\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:question\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Will graphics-card molecular simulations using Green–Kubo on C10–C50 hydrocarbons and esters rank immersion coolants' viscosity and thermal conductivity the same way measurements do?\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:hypothesis\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Green–Kubo MD with one fixed force field has a chemistry-dependent error floor near 25 percent that more molecules cannot remove [s_ogbomo_res].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_res\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_lever\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"At 120 molecules, held-out viscosity error after bias correction falls below 15 percent and rank correlation with measurement exceeds 0.9 [s_ogbomo_res].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_res\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_not\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Held-out viscosity error stays above 25 percent and rank correlation below 0.7 at every set size, capping candidate ranking [s_ogbomo_res].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_res\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:test_summary\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"One LAMMPS LOPLS-AA Green–Kubo protocol at 40 °C, six five-nanosecond replicas per molecule, run on 8, 24, 48 then 120 molecules from the public 835-molecule reference set, scored only against measured viscosity and thermal conductivity [s_ogbomo_db].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_db\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:closest_prior\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Ogbomo and colleagues, in 2026, used Green–Kubo molecular dynamics to compute viscosity and thermal conductivity for eight C10–C50 molecules at 40 °C and compared with measurements [s_ogbomo_md].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_md\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity.\\\"}],\\\"value\\\":8}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:left_open\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Whether the error is a correctable bias or a random floor that caps ranking, and how rank agreement holds over hundreds of molecules [s_ogbomo_db].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_db\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:anchor\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Repeat the published eight-molecule Green–Kubo run first: density within 4% for seven molecules and thermal conductivity over-predicted for all eight [s_ogbomo_res].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_ogbomo_res\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\\\"}],\\\"value\\\":\\\"density error 4% or less on 7 of 8 molecules at 40 °C\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:limits\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Shows transport-property error only at 40 °C for pure liquids between 1 and 50 mPa·s, not blends or sold coolants. Cannot show ranking behaviour beyond 120 molecules.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s_ogbomo_res\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"anchor tolerances, the predicted error floor and the if_not expectation\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s_ogbomo_db\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"the measured reference set used for scoring, its size and chemical range\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s_ogbomo_md\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity.\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"the closest prior work and the baseline arm of eight molecules\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:n_ref_molecules\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"molecules in the public reference set\\\",\\\"value\\\":835,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"molecules\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"reference dataset of measured density, viscosity and thermal conductivity at 40 and 100 °C\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:n_gpus\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"GPUs on the rented instance\\\",\\\"value\\\":8,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"GPUs\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Instances pricing (8x): NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU: 40 GB | vCPUs: 124 | RAM: 1800 GiB | STORAGE: 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.99\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Lambda on-demand 8-GPU A100 SXM 40 GB instance\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:a100x8_usd_gpu_h\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"price per GPU-hour, 8x A100 SXM 40 GB\\\",\\\"value\\\":1.99,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"USD/GPU-hour\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Instances pricing (8x): NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU: 40 GB | vCPUs: 124 | RAM: 1800 GiB | STORAGE: 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.99\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Lambda on-demand instance pricing read 2026-10-18\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:throughput_ns_day\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"assumed MD throughput per GPU\\\",\\\"value\\\":250,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"ns/day\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"PROXY\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 x A100 GPU:      |         ns/day =    611.08\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Amber JAC_PRODUCTION_NVE benchmark, 23,558 atoms, PME, 2 fs timestep, one A100 GPU\\\",\\\"differs_in\\\":[\\\"Amber pmemd.cuda rather than LAMMPS\\\",\\\"protein in water rather than neat organic liquid\\\",\\\"no per-step stress-tensor autocorrelation accumulation\\\",\\\"we take 250 ns/day as a safety factor of about 2.4 under the 611 ns/day figure\\\"],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://ambermd.org/GPUPerformance.php\\\"}\n\nReturn only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"array\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"One entry per item sent, with its ref unchanged.\\\",\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"ref\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"\\\\\"card:<field>\\\\\", \\\\\"src:<source id>\\\\\", \\\\\"num:<number id>\\\\\" or \\\\\"rate:<rate id>\\\\\", as sent.\\\"},\\\"status\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"enum\\\":[\\\"SUPPORTED\\\",\\\"PARTIAL\\\",\\\"UNSUPPORTED\\\",\\\"CONTRADICTED\\\",\\\"UNREACHABLE\\\"]},\\\"page_quote\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The text on the page this status rests on.\\\"},\\\"note\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"},\\\"page_value\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"number\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"num and rate items: the value the page states.\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"ref\\\",\\\"status\\\",\\\"page_quote\\\",\\\"note\\\"]}}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"items\\\"]}\""
