 across all three target properties. Out-of-distribution tests show that unreliable predictions can be flagged from descriptor-space distance and the position of the predicted value within the training range. Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity. At an inference cost orders of magnitude lower than EMD simulations, the ML models are well suited to high-throughput screening of new candidate molecules for lubricants and other formulated products.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Benchmarking Machine Learning and Molecular Dynamics Methods for the Prediction of the Thermophysical Properties of Organic Liquids\nURL: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20326213\nPublished: 2026-05-21T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: fionn-carman, Egheosa Ogbomo\nHighlights:\nfor density and thermal conductivity (40/100 C) and viscosity (40 C), plus verify.py for reproducing the test-set RMSE. PropertyPrediction/Scripts/: training scripts for all benchmarked model families. LAMMPS/: squalane equilibrium MD input files\n\n---\n\nTitle: Benchmarking Molecular Dynamics Simulations and Machine Learning Methods for Predicting Hydrocarbon Thermophysical Properties\nURL: https://doi.org/10.26434/chemrxiv.15002312/v1\nPublished: 2026-04-22T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: Egheosa Ogbomo, Fionn Carman, Daniele Dini, James Patrick Ewen\nHighlights:\nbase oils. We evaluate a range of ML architectures and molecular representations trained on ... accurately predict the thermophysical properties of unseen hydrocarbons. The computational cost of the ML models is several orders of magnitude\n\n---\n\nTitle: Our paper has now been published in Digital Discovery! 🚀\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/egheosa-ogbomo-phd-225143ab_benchmarking-machine-learning-and-molecular-activity-7513930301375401986-JghP\nPublished: 2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nIn the paper, we compiled approximately 4,700 reference values for 835 organic molecules and used the dataset to benchmark a range of machine learning methods against molecular dynamics simulations for predicting density, viscosity and thermal\n\n---\n\nTitle: I'm not a regular poster on LinkedIn, but this one is probably worth it. | Egheosa Ogbomo, PhD\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/egheosa-ogbomo-phd-225143ab_benchmarking-molecular-dynamics-simulations-activity-7452702005871112192-nGml\nPublished: 2026-04-22T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: Egheosa Ogbomo, PhD\nHighlights:\nOver the course of 18 months during my PhD, we collated 5,500+ experimental data points for ~1,200 hydrocarbons (manually!!), using this data to benchmark various machine learning models against molecular dynamics simulations for predicting density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity."
